@* When an activity's encounter happened, as a list cell (T137, from T119's ObservedOn). A date nobody stated is only
   the day the form was filed, and it says so rather than passing the audit clock off as a clinical fact. The
   explanation is visible text, not a tooltip: a keyboard, touch or screen-reader user never sees a title. *@
@if (Declared)
{
  <span>@Formatted</span>
}
else
{
  <span class="muted">@Formatted (filed; no encounter date)</span>
}

@code {
  [Parameter, EditorRequired] public DateOnly ObservedOn { get; set; }
  [Parameter] public bool Declared { get; set; }

  private string Formatted => ObservedOn.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
}
